# The staging build's settings: staging.jackioh.com, behind Cloudflare Access, which
# deploy-staging.yml deploys from main. `build:staging` (package.json) loads this file into the
# build's environment, so each value here wins over .env.production's and MODE stays `production`.
# .env.production's rules hold here too: every value is public, env-production.test.ts holds this
# file to the same keys and refusals (and to every key .env.production sets, so none of production's
# reaches staging), and `check-production-bundle.mjs --staging` refuses a bundle missing any of them.
#
# Supabase: staging's own project, JackiOh-Staging: the original project, which production left for
# JackiOh-Production (docs/deploy-cloudflare.md section 8). The development lanes file here too.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://exmjdaswedxhnzmpzqrq.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_tNmTI9vMGC9_YCiubVtFDw_A2e50TTx
# The server shares the site's origin: wrangler.jsonc's env.staging sends /api/* and /ws/* to it.
VITE_SERVER_HTTP_URL=https://staging.jackioh.com
VITE_SERVER_WS_URL=wss://staging.jackioh.com/ws/match
# #696: the address staging is served from (net/navigate.ts SITE_ORIGIN, which the source files spell).
VITE_SITE_ORIGIN=https://staging.jackioh.com
